        "essence_text": "A sensory avalanche that treats laundry, taxes, and the fate of every possible life as equally urgent. It ricochets from slapstick and genre pastiche into crushing tenderness without losing its emotional compass. The experience is less about following a plot than riding a feeling of infinite possibility colliding with ordinary love. When the noise finally stills, what remains is a stubborn, almost radical insistence on kindness. It leaves you breathless, bewildered, and unexpectedly held."
